   "page": 83,
   "box": 0,
   "kind_hint": "outside",
   "section": null,
   "section_y": -1,
   "indent": 0,
   "parent": null,
   "text": "• Give cefalexin 500mg 6 hourly or flucloxacillin 500mg 6 hourly for 5 days. If severe penicillin allergy1, give instead azithromycin 500mg daily for 3 days. • Give paracetamol 500mg-1g 4-6 hourly (up to 4g in 24 hours) as needed for up to 5 days. • If limb affected, advise to keep elevated. • Refer same day if: - BP < 90/60 - Pulse > 100 - Confused - Hand, face or scalp involvement - Extensive infection - Blisters or grey/black skin - Poorly controlled diabetes - Recurrent infections with underlying problem (like lymphoedema) - No response to treatment within 2 days.",
